# LF in the working tree on every platform. The Windows runner checks out under
# git's core.autocrlf=true, so without this every text file arrives CRLF and
# `prettier --check` refuses the whole tree - 61 of 61 files on run 33822348514,
# which is what actually reddened the windows-2025 leg of the 0.1.0 release.
# Normalising the checkout rather than relaxing prettier's `endOfLine` keeps one
# line ending in the repository, the working tree and the packed tarball, and
# leaves the formatter free to keep saying what it sees.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The house design system's files are upstream's bytes, pinned by SHA-256 in
# src/browser/house/pin.json; IBM Plex Mono's OFL.txt is CRLF upstream, and
# normalising it would fail test/house.test.js on every fresh checkout.
src/browser/house/** -text
